# Typography: Language on a box in another language, and its letter rules with Case: uppercase.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Typography · Language
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: quote
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
				Padding: 8 12
				Border: 0 0 0 3
				Border color: accent
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Italic: true
				Size: 12
		For style: upper
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
			Typography:
				Case: uppercase
				Size: 14
	Section:
		Text: Typography
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Language
		Paragraph: The language of the document is its `Language`. A box in another language declares its own in `Typography`: a screen reader changes voice there, and hyphenation and automatic capitals follow its rules. The language belongs to the whole box.
			Style: intro
		Text: Typography: Language: fr
			Style: label
		Paragraph: « Je pense, donc je suis », écrit Descartes dans le Discours de la méthode.
			Style: quote
			Typography:
				Language: fr
		Text: Typography: Language: ca
			Style: label
		Paragraph: La plaça s'omple de castanyes cada tardor, i el mercat obre fins al vespre.
			Style: quote
			Typography:
				Language: ca
		Text: Case: uppercase on the word "istanbul", painted by the rules of each language
			Style: label
		Text: en: istanbul
			Style: upper
		Text: tr: istanbul
			Style: upper
			Typography:
				Language: tr
